Sure! Below is a simple example of a rotating card using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it will rotate 180 degrees around its Y‑axis.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
  /* Container to center the card */
  .card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives a 3D effect */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
  }

  /* The card itself */
  .card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Keep 3D children */
    position: relative;
  }

  /* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
  .card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }

  /* Front and back faces */
  .card-face {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide back face when rotated */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #333;
  }

  .card-front {
    background: #f8f9fa;
  }

  .card-back {
    background: #e9ecef;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Flip back face so it shows on hover */
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      <p>Front side – Hover me!</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      <p>Back side – Rotated!</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works
- **`perspective`** on the wrapper gives depth to the 3D rotation.
- **`transform-style: preserve-3d`** keeps child elements in 3D space.
- **`backface-visibility: hidden`** hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away.
- On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face.

Feel free to customize colors, text, or add more content inside the faces. Enjoy!
